((intellect3-math
  ((question . "A sequence $a_1$, $a_2$, $\\ldots$ of non-negative integers is defined by the rule $a_{n+2}=|a_{n+1}-a_n|$ for $n\\geq1$. If $a_1=999$, $a_2<999$, and $a_{2006}=1$, how many different values of $a_2$ are possible?")
    (answer . "324")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "6.12 friends have a weekly dinner together, each week they are divided into three groups, each group 4 people, and different groups sit at different tables. If it is required that any two of these friends sit at the same table at least once, then at least how many weeks are needed.")
    (answer . "5")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "Consider the following two strings of digits: $11001010100101011$ and $110100011000100$. First consider them to be in base $10$ and sum them to get $n$. Then consider them to be in binary, sum them, write the answer in binary, then interpret the digits of the sum as if they were in base $10$ to get $m$. What is $n-m$?")
    (answer . "0")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "There are \\(n\\) lilypads in a row labeled \\(1,2,\\dots,n\\). Fareniss the Frog picks a lilypad at random to start on and jumps every second to an adjacent lilypad; if there are two choices, she is twice as likely to jump to the right. After some time, there exist two lilypads \\(A\\) and \\(B\\) such that the probability of being on \\(A\\) is more than 1000 times that of \\(B\\). What is the minimal \\(n\\) for which this must occur?")
    (answer . "12")
    (difficulty . "0.5"))
  ((question . "Kevin colors three distinct squares in a  $3\\times 3$  grid red. Given that there exist two uncolored squares such that coloring one of them would create a horizontal or vertical red line, find the number of ways he could have colored the original three squares.")
    (answer . "36")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "8. (10 points) Through a point $P$ inside an equilateral triangle $A B C$, perpendiculars are drawn to the three sides, with the feet of the perpendiculars being $D, E, F$ respectively. Connect $A P$, $B P$, $C P$. If the area of the equilateral triangle $A B C$ is 2028 square centimeters, and the areas of triangles $P A D$ and $P B E$ are both 192 square centimeters, then the area of triangle $P C F$ is $\\qquad$ square centimeters.")
    (answer . "630")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "On the lateral side \\( CD \\) of the trapezoid \\( ABCD (AD \\parallel BC) \\), point \\( M \\) is marked. From vertex \\( A \\), a perpendicular \\( AH \\) is dropped onto segment \\( BM \\). It turns out that \\( AD = HD \\). Find the length of segment \\( AD \\) if it is known that \\( BC = 16 \\), \\( CM = 8 \\), and \\( MD = 9 \\).")
    (answer . "18")
    (difficulty . "0.375"))
  ((question . "A semicircle with diameter  $d$  is contained in a square whose sides have length  $8$ . Given the maximum value of  $d$  is  $m- \\sqrt{n}$ , find  $m+n$ .")
    (answer . "544")
    (difficulty . "0.25"))
  ((question . "Find the smallest possible value of $n$ such that $n+2$ people can stand inside or on the border of a regular $n$-gon with side length $6$ feet where each pair of people are at least $6$ feet apart.")
    (answer . "10")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "In trapezoid $K L M N$, the bases $K N$ and $L M$ are equal to 12 and 3, respectively. From point $Q$, lying on side $M N$, a perpendicular $Q P$ is dropped to side $K L$. It is known that $P$ is the midpoint of side $K L$, $P M=4$, and that the area of quadrilateral $P L M Q$ is four times smaller than the area of quadrilateral $P K N Q$.\n\nFind the length of segment $P N$.")
    (answer . "16")
    (difficulty . "0.5"))
))
